# Memory Vessel: "{T}, Exile this artifact: Each player exiles the top seven cards of their library. Until your next turn, players may
# play cards they exiled this way, and they can't play cards from their hand. Activate only as a sorcery." (CR 406, 305.1, 601.3,
# 611.2a, 101.2). Bot1 casts it on turn 1 and activates it: both libraries lose seven cards to exile, nothing in either hand can be
# played (not Bot1's Mountain, and on turn 2 neither Bot2's Mox Ruby nor the Mountain it drew), while the exiled cards can: Bot1 plays
# a Mountain from exile as its land drop and casts the exiled Mox Jet and taps it for mana, and on Bot2's turn the exiled Mox
# Emerald, Mox Jet, Forest and Grizzly Bears are played the same way. Once Bot1's turn 3 begins the permission is gone (Bot2's Island
# left in exile can't be played on turn 4, Bot1's exiled Mountain can't), and the hand rule is gone too (a Mountain from hand is played).

